{"slug": "instrument-index-document-guide", "targets": ["instrument index"], "html": "<h2 style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:700;color:#0186e0;margin:34px 0 16px;\">Instrument Index Sample Entries for Common Device Types</h2><p><strong>Instrument index</strong> rows look different for each kind of device, and new engineers often ask what a filled in row actually looks like. The table below shows typical sample entries for one small loop area, using ISA 5.1 style tags, so you can see how type, signal and I/O columns change from one instrument to the next.</p><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\"><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:14px 0;font-size:16px;\"><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Tag</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Service</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Instrument type</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Signal</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">I/O type</th></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">FT 101</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Feed flow to reactor</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Magnetic flow transmitter</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">4 to 20 mA HART</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">AI</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">FV 101</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Feed flow control</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Control valve with positioner</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">4 to 20 mA</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">AO</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">TT 102</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Reactor temperature</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">RTD with head transmitter</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">4 to 20 mA HART</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">AI</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">LSH 103</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Tank level high</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Vibrating fork switch</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Dry contact</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">DI</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">XV 104</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Tank outlet isolation</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">On off valve with solenoid</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">24 V DC</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">DO</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">ZSC 104</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">XV 104 closed feedback</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Limit switch</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Dry contact</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">DI</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">PG 105</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Pump discharge pressure</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Local pressure gauge</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">None</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">No I/O</td></tr></table></div><h3 style=\"font-size:19px;font-weight:700;color:#1a2b4a;margin:20px 0 10px;\">Tips for Filling the Rows</h3><ol><li>Copy the tag exactly as shown on the P&ID, including loop number and suffix.</li><li>Write the service in plain words an operator would recognise.</li><li>Enter local gauges too, even though they take no I/O channel.</li><li>Give limit switches their own rows so the DI count stays correct.</li><li>Mark each row with its revision so changes can be traced.</li></ol>"}